Sat Nov 07 17:00:00 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Start thermald only on Intel CPUs. On AMD it logged "Unsupported cpu
  model or platform" and exited on every boot.
- Release 19. The repository already has 0.4.0-18.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Nov 07 15:00:00 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Ship atropos-ssh-agent.service, a user ssh-agent on the socket that
  SSH_AUTH_SOCK names. openSUSE's openssh has no user unit, so the
  socket did not exist and ssh-add failed.
- Install 11-atropos-performance.conf in /etc/sysctl.d. tuned reapplies
  only /run and /etc/sysctl.d after a profile, so the Performance power
  profile left vm.swappiness at 10 and vm.dirty_ratio at 40. Pin the
  writeback ratios to the kernel defaults there as well.
- Configure the Firefox Flatpak from "flatpak info --show-runtime". The
  "Runtime:" label is translated, so in German and other locales the
  files went to a directory Firefox does not read. Remove that
  directory.
- Mount the Discover About page overlay only over the exact
  kirigami-addons6 1.14.0 files it was made from. Every host KDE
  application loads that module. Copy to Clipboard uses KDeclarative's
  Clipboard type instead of a D-Bus call to Klipper.
- Retry the first-boot Flatpak download every few minutes until it
  works. An offline first boot left the desktop without Firefox until
  the next boot. Welcome Center says it is waiting for a connection.
- Run powertop --auto-tune only on a machine with a system battery,
  and keep USB audio, Bluetooth and USB network adapters awake too.
- Write the systemd-boot timeout variable only when it changes.
- Find the LUKS mapping's device instead of assuming dm-0, and do
  nothing without encryption.
- Do not reload udev on the running system from inside
  transactional-update.
- Release 18. The repository already has 0.4.0-17.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Nov 04 00:29:06 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Turn IOMMU passthrough off and disable kexec on the kernel command
  line. kernel-longterm defaults to passthrough, and the kexec sysctl
  only applies after userspace starts.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 08:36:59 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Seed Merkuro, Elisa, Skanlite, and KMahjongg from Flathub.
- Welcome Center said the Flatpak download had finished while the
  seed service was still going to run, and then stopped checking.
  The progress page stays up until that service has exited, and it
  keeps checking so a late start is shown.
- A fresh install no longer downloads those applications from the
  package script. The first-boot service does it while Welcome
  Center can see it.

